WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:04.410
SPEAKER 1: Spinnaker for Google
Cloud Platform is a solution

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:06.420
that lets you
install Spinnaker--

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:09.690
the open-source multi-cloud
application delivery platform--

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:11.370
in Google Cloud
Platform with a couple

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:13.650
of clicks to start
creating pipelines

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:17.392
for continuous delivery
of your applications.

00:00:17.392 --> 00:00:19.350
When you open the management
environment, which

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:22.890
runs in Cloud Shell, you can
follow a set of guided steps

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:24.810
to install a
production-ready Spinnaker

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:27.240
instance in a new Google
Kubernetes Engine cluster

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:31.410
in minutes using Google's
recommended settings.

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:33.690
You can change many of the
installation parameters

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:37.645
if desired, including installing
Spinnaker in an existing GKE

00:00:37.645 --> 00:00:38.145
cluster.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:43.440
Spinnaker for Google
Cloud Platform

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:45.510
also integrates your
Spinnaker installation

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:47.700
with other Google
Cloud Services,

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:53.610
such as Cloud Build, Container
Registry, and Stackdriver.

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:56.040
Once the installation
process is complete,

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:59.550
you can access the Spinnaker
UI via port forwarding

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:01.710
or automatically configure
a secured endpoint

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:05.888
using Cloud Identity-Aware Proxy
with a valid SSL certificate.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:20.050
The management environment
provides many helpers

00:01:20.050 --> 00:01:22.060
to simplify ongoing
administration

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:24.490
of your Spinnaker instances.

00:01:24.490 --> 00:01:26.080
The configuration
of each instance

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:28.600
is automatically and
securely backed up

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:32.710
for auditing and fast recovery.

00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:37.160
Helpers are provided to connect
Spinnaker to new GKE clusters

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:39.460
and to create accounts to
deploy to Google Compute

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:43.300
Engine, and Google App Engine,
and other GCP projects.

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:44.800
You will also have
access to the hal

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:46.870
and spin command line
tools, giving you

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:50.710
full control of your
Spinnaker instances if needed.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:53.290
The solution lets you add sample
pipelines and applications

00:01:53.290 --> 00:01:54.850
to Spinnaker that
demonstrate best

00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:58.720
practices for deployments to
Kubernetes, VMs, and more.

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:00.940
DevOps teams can use
these as starting points

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:04.060
to provide golden path
deployment pipelines tailored

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:06.820
to their company's requirements.

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:09.610
The Hello World web
application, for example,

00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:11.800
demonstrates a
continuous delivery setup

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:14.200
that builds the application
with Cloud Build,

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.360
and deploys it first
to staging, and then

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:18.539
to production with Spinnaker.

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:38.430
Once the staging
deployment is completed,

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:40.760
a manual judgment determines
whether to continue

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:43.160
with the deployment
to production.

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:44.770
Spinnaker for Google
Cloud Platform

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:48.050
is pre-integrated with Google
Pub/Sub for notifications

00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:51.365
and can also be linked to Slack,
email, and other notification

00:02:51.365 --> 00:02:51.865
channels.

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:02.500
The deployment to production
demonstrates a number

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:04.990
of good practices, such
as automated rollback

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:08.290
when the validation tests fail
and the hot standby period

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:11.045
after successful validation
in case something unexpected

00:03:11.045 --> 00:03:11.545
happens.

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:23.470
We can see the
Kubernetes resources

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:26.050
Spinnaker is managing
in the Spinnaker UI

00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:27.820
and can go straight
to our deployed app

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:28.690
to check things out.

00:03:31.912 --> 00:03:33.370
You can try out
the solution today.

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:35.950
Just search for Spinnaker
for Google Cloud Platform

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:37.320
on cloud.google.com

